llama.cpp is vendored as the `vendor/llama.cpp` git submodule and is the
foundation of this project: learning-llamas compiles a C shim against its private
`src/` internals, and code is copied and adapted from it into `csrc/` and into
project-authored ggml kernels.

Every file in this repository containing code copied or adapted from llama.cpp
carries a provenance header naming the source path, the source commit, and the
license. See docs/PROVENANCE.md for the policy and the header template.

